# Nothing game-derived may enter git history.
#
# The game's code and assets are copyrighted, and anything produced by feeding
# them through the recompiler is a derivative of them. Only original work --
# the scaffold, tools, configuration, reports and build files -- belongs here.
# A game-derived file committed once has to be purged from history, not just
# the working tree, so keep it out in the first place.

# Extracted contents of the user's own disc image.
game_files/

# Lifted from the game by tools.recomp: derivative, regenerable with
# ./regenerate.sh from the user's own copy.
src/recomp/gen/

# Pipeline intermediates (disasm/func_id/abi_analysis output). These are
# game-derived and fully reproducible; they are deliberately kept inside this
# workspace rather than in /mnt/dev/xboxrecomp-fork so a run leaves the shared
# toolchain worktree untouched.
build/

# Build output, including the compiled game code.
build-*/
*.exe
*.dll
*.a
*.o
*.obj

# Runtime artefacts from a debug run.
*.log
backtrace*.txt
icall_targets.dump

# Frame dumps: game-derived rendered output.
framedump_*.ppm

# CodeGraph's local index.
.codegraph/

# Research: the WRITTEN work is tracked (research/reports, research/README.md),
# because that is original analysis. The evidence it cites is not, because it
# is game-derived:
#
#   research/artifacts/  a copy of default.xbe, sampled .dff/.dds/.raw/.dat/
#                        .cfg disc files, dsstdfx.bin, and bulk string dumps
#                        pulled out of the executable -- all verbatim game
#                        content or direct extractions of it;
#   research/captures/   screenshots of the running game;
#   research/xemu-profile/  machine-local emulator state.
#
# These stay durable on disk and HeroLab records their exact paths and the
# commands that recreate them; they just never enter git history, where a
# mistake cannot be undone by deleting the file.
# Note the trailing /* rather than /: git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so a negation below it would never be reached.
research/artifacts/*
research/captures/
research/xemu-profile/

# Exception: tool-generated measurements about the executable (function counts
# per section, import call counts). Our own output, no game content.
!research/artifacts/phase1/

# Python bytecode.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The Windows launcher's build output (launcher-win/build.sh).
launcher-win/out/
